{"action_id":"a0002","additional_user_input":[],"audience":"unspecified","constraints":[],"context":null,"goal":null,"inputs":{"draft":{"answer":"For x≠2, (x²−4)/(x−2)=x+2. The original expression has domain ℝ\\{2}. The simplified expression x+2 is defined for every real x, so it is not equivalent to the original at every real number: at x=2 it equals 4 whereas the original is undefined.","approaches":[{"description":"Factor the numerator as a difference of squares and cancel the common nonzero factor on the original domain.","id":"factor-cancel","outcome":"candidate","reason":"This directly establishes the simplification and preserves the excluded value."}],"change_log":[],"claims":[{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived in factor-step and cancel-step.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"factorization","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"x²−4=(x−2)(x+2) for every real x.","step_ids":["factor-step"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived in domain-step.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"original-domain","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The domain of (x²−4)/(x−2) is ℝ\\{2}.","step_ids":["domain-step"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived in cancel-step using factorization and the original-domain claim.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["factorization","original-domain"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"simplification","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"On its domain, (x²−4)/(x−2)=x+2.","step_ids":["cancel-step"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived in non-equivalence-step.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["original-domain","simplification"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"not-global-equivalence","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The simplified expression x+2 is not equivalent to the original expression at every real number.","step_ids":["non-equivalence-step"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":[],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"factor-step","justification":"Expanding (x−2)(x+2) gives x²−4.","statement":"Factor the numerator: x²−4=(x−2)(x+2)."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"domain-step","justification":"A quotient is defined only when its denominator is nonzero; x−2=0 exactly when x=2.","statement":"The original expression is defined exactly for x≠2."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["factor-step","domain-step"],"id":"cancel-step","justification":"For x≠2, the factor x−2 is nonzero and may be cancelled: ((x−2)(x+2))/(x−2)=x+2.","statement":"On ℝ\\{2}, the expression simplifies to x+2."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["domain-step","cancel-step"],"id":"non-equivalence-step","justification":"At x=2, x+2=4 is defined, but the original quotient has zero denominator and is undefined.","statement":"The two expressions do not have the same value-status at every real number."}],"question_status":"answered","tool_requests":[]},"draft_id":"a0001"},"objective":"prove","output_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"challenges":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"attack":{"maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"claim_id":{"maxLength":64,"pattern":"[a-z][a-z0-9-]{2,63}","type":"string"},"outcome":{"enum":["survives","fails","not_tested"],"type":"string"},"result":{"maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"tool_ids":{"items":{"maxLength":64,"pattern":"[a-z][a-z0-9-]{2,63}","type":"string"},"maxItems":4,"type":"array"}},"required":["claim_id","attack","result","outcome","tool_ids"],"type":"object"},"maxItems":12,"type":"array"},"checks":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"basis_reasoning":{"maxLength":4000,"type":"string"},"basis_verdict":{"enum":["applicable","not_applicable","unsupported","conditional","source_attributed","not_tested"],"type":"string"},"checked_step_ids":{"items":{"maxLength":64,"pattern"